# platform retro r1 — Claude Opus 5 (1M context)

## Summary (≤5 lines)
- 40 ranked tasks; the dominant waste is infra rounds, not code difficulty.
- Three tasks needed a re-dispatch after a transient provider 429.
- The fixer WIP slot idled for roughly a third of the window.

## Findings (ranked, ≤6)
- Finding 1: infra rounds outnumber code rounds 3:1 on the worst-ranked tasks.
- Finding 2: two tasks re-fetched the same ledger slice from cold cache.
- Finding 3: the argv ceiling warn band fired twice, never crossed.
- Finding 4: one goose cell died clean on a provider retry, unnoticed by exit code.
- Finding 5: the harvest's slug derivation collided once on a harness A/B run.
- Finding 6: no report floor existed before this run — the direct cause of this fixture's sibling.

## Proposed process changes
- Cache the ledger slice per run, not per task: cuts the cold-cache refetch to zero.
- Pin the goose provider retry to a bounded backoff instead of an instant clean exit.
- Add a content floor to the marker self-check, not just a non-empty check.

## Task granularity
- Task 12 was chunked right: one round, clean report, no rework.
- Task 19 should have been split: three rounds against one file, evidence of thrash.
- Task 24 fan-out was correct: three independent files, three clean rounds in parallel.

## Wins to codify
- The argv guard's warn band caught a growing brief before it hit the ceiling.
- The per-cell OpenRouter key mint kept a dead cell's spend off the fixer budget.

## Platform KPIs
- bucket-A count 4, jail $/day 1.10, trend flat, next gate unchanged.

## Predecessor score
- No merged predecessor changes this run.

## Evidence confidence
- Could not verify the pushgateway metric directly; inferred from the PR timestamps.
